// Trail feature catalog (TrailFeatureType). Copied into the world when a scenario starts, so saves are self-contained.
// A feature covers lengthMeters of a trail from where it is placed. Every covered ~10 m segment must lie within the
// gradient window (tenths of the -10..+10 score along the direction of travel: -50 = -5.0 = 45° down), and at least one
// must turn by minTurn (segment turn permille: 100 ≈ 37°). Difficulty (0..1000) raises the covered segments and sets a
// floor for the trail's rating (green < 250 <= blue < 480 <= red < 700 <= black): berms, rollers and tables fit a blue
// trail; wooden kickers, wall-rides and small drops make it red; doubles (later rock gardens, long jumps) black. Affinities (0..1000) say how much
// flow and technical riders enjoy it; funWeight is how many fun samples one pass counts as (a segment counts one).
// Building one is a crew job: workMinutes crew-minutes at base speed (digging for dirt, carpentry for wood) and wood
// units taken from the stock when work starts.
